-- Update only the unedited starting brief; keep personal edits and archived favourites.
UPDATE design_entries SET content=json_set(content,'$.text','Develop the selected Social kitchen across the full confirmed A+B+C volume. A is the long WEST extension with an eight-seat dining table running north–south. B is the shallow NORTH return with one sofa and a coffee table. C is the enlarged original kitchen with a generous freestanding oak island running north–south; D, the cooker, stays on its EAST wall. Open the former west and north boundaries around retained piers as a structural proposal. Keep the confirmed outline and proportions: do not rotate, mirror, deepen B or enlarge the envelope. Use the Social kitchen plan and fixed spatial model to control geometry. Explore pale oak, limestone, sage range cabinetry, slim dark glazing and a low insulated extension roof with oak soffits; retain the original white kitchen ceiling. Use the original interior and garden photographs for views and distinguish photo-based views from inferred new viewpoints. AI images convey atmosphere and finishes; they do not establish dimensions, roof or structure. The alternative layouts remain in the archive. Furniture fit, openings, ceiling heights, services and the actual approved drawings remain to be verified.'),version=version+1,updated_at=strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now') WHERE project='kitchen' AND kind='brief' AND json_extract(content,'$.text')='Treat A+B+C as one year-round kitchen, dining and living volume. A is the long west extension, B the shallow north return, C the existing kitchen, and D the existing east cooker wall. Use the confirmed source-plan outline and proportions in every option; do not rotate, mirror, deepen B or enlarge the envelope. Compare three layouts: a larger social kitchen in C with dining in A and lounging in B; a relocated working kitchen in A with dining in C and breakfast in B; and a family lounge in A with dining at the northwest corner and a redesigned kitchen in C. The island and cooker may move where the selected plan explicitly proposes it. Wider north and west openings are proposals, with retained piers shown as assumptions pending structural review. Follow each selected plan and deterministic cutaway model before using its AI illustration as a finish reference. Use warm timber, limestone, slim glazing and the natural character of the house. Furniture fit, ceiling height, supports and service routes are not verified. Actual approved drawings and measured dimensions remain outstanding.';
